  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "DngOpcodes::OffsetPerRowOrCol::apply",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/common/DngOpcodes.cpp",
    "description": "Heap OOB read is caused by indexing delta arrays with absolute pixel coordinates (`S::select(x,y)` returning x for DeltaPerColumn) without validating that the opcode-provided delta table length matches the traversed ROI coordinate range. In `OffsetPerRowOrCol::apply`, `this->deltaI[S::select(x,y)]` / `this->deltaF[...]` can read past the vector when x (or y for row variant) exceeds `deltaF_count` parsed in `DeltaRowOrCol` constructor. Crash manifests in `OffsetPerRowOrCol<...SelectX>::apply` but root cause is missing bounds/consistency check between ROI dimensions and delta table size for DeltaPerColumn opcode data.",
    "conditions": "PoV supplies a DNG opcode list (stage1 via OPCODELIST1 in `DngDecoder::handleMetadata`) containing DeltaPerColumn (opcode 11) with too-short `deltaF_count`. During `DngOpcodes::applyOpCodes`, the opcode is set up and applied over ROI pixels; loop uses image x coordinates, so when ROI width/image width is larger than delta table length, out-of-bounds vector access occurs, producing ASan heap-buffer-overflow read."
  },
